XCOMM
XCOMM comcomp -- spikes toward a ComTerp-to-Go compiler; see each
XCOMM subdirectory's own README.md. builtin_poc needs a Go toolchain
XCOMM (go build -buildmode=c-archive) and is deliberately NOT in the
XCOMM default SUBDIRS chain, so a normal build doesn't require Go --
XCOMM build it directly: cd builtin_poc && make Makefiles && make.
XCOMM examples IS in the chain (its own Imakefile needs no Go, and
XCOMM its Go-generating rule isn't hooked to the "all" target, so it
XCOMM stays inert during a normal build -- see its own Imakefile).
XCOMM

PACKAGE = comcomp

InstallScriptAs(comcomp,$(BINDIR),comcomp)
InstallScript(funccompile.comt,$(BINDIR))

SUBDIRS = \
	examples

MakeInSubdirs($(SUBDIRS))
